    <miscellaneous>
      <miscellaneous-field name="editorial-footnote-a-bar31">(a) If this one (superfluous?) note were eliminated, the piece would take on a more normal rhythmical pattern, starting with the up-beat. Schumann was probably inspired by the Scherzo in Beethoven's op. 24. But Beethoven's notation, for various reasons, does not admit of any alteration.</miscellaneous-field>
    </miscellaneous>
  </identification>
